Sawal 1: Kaunse Patterns Django Mein Already Handled Hain?
1. Singleton
Kya hai: Ek aisi class jiska sirf ek hi object poori application mein bane, bar bar naya na banaya jaye.
Django mein kahan: settings.py file — jab tum from django.conf import settings karte ho, Django poori application mein ek hi settings object deta hai, har jagah wahi instance use hota hai. Naya banane ki zaroorat nahi.
Kyun already handled hai: Django ka apps registry aur settings loader internally isko manage karta hai — tumhe koi Singleton class khud likhne ki zaroorat nahi.
2. Factory Method
Kya hai: Ek aisa mechanism jo tumhare liye object "bana kar" de, bina tumhe manually constructor call kiye.
Django mein kahan: DRF Serializer — JobSerializer(data=request.data) likhte hi, ek validated Job object "factory" ki tarah ban jata hai.
Kyun already handled hai: Tumhe khud se "if valid then create object" wala logic nahi likhna — Serializer class yeh internally karti hai.
3. Builder
Kya hai: Complex object ko step by step pieces jorh kar banane ka tareeqa.
Django mein kahan: QuerySet chaining — Job.objects.filter(status='published').exclude(location='Karachi').order_by('-created_at')
Kyun already handled hai: Har .filter(), .exclude() ek step add karta hai final query mein — yeh exactly Builder pattern hai, jo Django ka ORM khud implement kar chuka hai.
4. Decorator
Kya hai: Kisi function/class ko bina uska original code chede, extra behavior "wrap" kar dena.
Django mein kahan: @permission_classes([IsAuthenticated]), @api_view(['GET'])
Kyun already handled hai: Yeh Python ka decorator syntax hai jo DRF use karta hai — tumhe manually koi wrapper class likhne ki zaroorat nahi.
5. Template Method
Kya hai: Ek base class jo poora process ka skeleton define kare, aur sirf kuch specific steps child class mein override hon.
Django mein kahan: Tumhare JobDetailView(APIView) mein get(), put(), delete() — base APIView class ka dispatch() method already decide karta hai request kaise route hogi, authentication kab check hogi. Tum sirf specific action (get/put/delete) likhte ho.
Kyun already handled hai: Poora request-handling flow (authentication → permission check → method call) already APIView mein defined hai.
6. Chain of Responsibility
Kya hai: Ek request multiple handlers se guzarti hai, har handler apna kaam kar ke aage bhej deta hai.
Django mein kahan: MIDDLEWARE list settings.py mein — request pehle CORS middleware se guzarti hai, phir Auth middleware, phir Session middleware, phir view tak pohanchti hai.
Kyun already handled hai: Middleware order settings.py mein already Django khud manage karta hai.
7. Observer
Kya hai: Jab ek event ho, to multiple "listeners" automatically trigger ho jayein.
Django mein kahan: Signals — post_save signal. Jaise hi ek Job create hoti hai, tum @receiver(post_save, sender=Job) se listener laga sakte ho jo automatically email bhej de.
Kyun already handled hai: Signal dispatch mechanism Django ka core feature hai, tumhe khud event system banane ki zaroorat nahi.
8. Iterator
Kya hai: Kisi collection ke items pe ek ek karke loop chalane ka standard tareeqa.
Django mein kahan: for job in Job.objects.all(): — QuerySet Python ke iterator protocol ko follow karta hai.
Kyun already handled hai: Tumhe khud __next__() method wagera likhne ki zaroorat nahi, QuerySet already iterable hai.
9. Proxy (Partial)
Kya hai: Ek object jo asal object ka "substitute" ban ke kaam kare, jaise lazy loading.
Django mein kahan: Job.objects.filter(status='draft') likhne se turant database query nahi chalti — jab tak tum usko iterate ya print na karo, wo sirf ek "lazy QuerySet object" rehta hai.
Kyun already handled hai: Yeh Django ORM ka internal optimization hai (lazy evaluation), tumhe manually implement nahi karna.

Sawal 2: Kaunse Patterns Manually Implement Karne Chahiye?
1. Strategy
Kya hai: Ek hi kaam ke liye multiple tareeqe (algorithms) ho, aur runtime pe decide ho kaunsa use karna hai.
Job Board mein example: Notification bhejna — kabhi email se, kabhi SMS se. Har channel ek alag "strategy class" ho:
pythonclass EmailNotification:
    def send(self, msg): ...
class SMSNotification:
    def send(self, msg): ...
Kyun manually: Django khud yeh decision nahi leta ke tumhare business ko konsa notification channel chahiye — yeh tumhari apni logic hai.
2. Facade
Kya hai: Complex, multiple-step process ko ek simple interface ke peeche chhupa dena.
Job Board mein example: Job apply karna — duplicate check + application create + email bhejna, teeno steps ek JobApplicationService.apply() function mein wrap kar do. View sirf ek line likhe:
pythonJobApplicationService().apply(request.user, job)
Kyun manually: Yeh tumhari business process hai, Django ka koi built-in "apply flow" nahi hota.
3. Adapter
Kya hai: Do incompatible interfaces ke beech "translator" ka kaam karna.
Job Board mein example: Agar LinkedIn Jobs API se data lena ho, unka JSON format tumhare Job model se match nahi karega. Ek Adapter class banao jo unka format tumhare format mein convert kare.
Kyun manually: Third-party API ka format tum control nahi kar sakte, isliye translation layer khud likhni padegi.
4. Command
Kya hai: Har action ko ek object ki tarah treat karna, jise queue mein daala ja sake, undo kiya ja sake, ya baad mein execute kiya ja sake.
Job Board mein example: Celery async task — "SendJobAlertCommand" jo background mein subscribers ko email bheje.
Kyun manually: Django khud "task queue" system nahi deta (Celery separate library hai), isliye yeh manually design karna padta hai.
5. State
Kya hai: Object ka behavior uske current state ke mutabiq badalna.
Job Board mein example: Job ka status — draft → published → closed → archived. Har state mein different actions allowed hone chahiye (jaise closed job pe apply na ho sake).
Kyun manually: Django ka status field sirf ek text/choice field hota hai — actual transition rules aur validation logic (draft se seedha archived nahi ja sakta) tumhe khud likhni hoti hai.
6. Memento
Kya hai: Object ka purana snapshot save karna taake baad mein undo/rollback ho sake.
Job Board mein example: Job update karne se pehle purani values save kar lena (audit trail/history feature ke liye).
Kyun manually: Django khud versioning system nahi deta (jab tak alag package use na karo), yeh manually implement karna padta hai.
7. Mediator
Kya hai: Multiple objects/services aapas mein directly baat na karein, balke ek beech wala coordinator unke through communicate kare.
Job Board mein example: Jab job create ho, to Notification service, Analytics service, aur Search-index service teeno ko update karna ho — ek Mediator class in teeno ko coordinate kare taake Job model khud in teeno se directly coupled na ho.
Kyun manually: Yeh pure business-specific coordination hai, Django ka koi built-in mediator nahi hota.
8. Prototype
Kya hai: Naya object banane ke bajaye, existing object ko clone karke thoda modify kar lena.
Job Board mein example: Company rep ek purani job posting ko template ki tarah copy kar ke naya similar job jaldi bana le.
Kyun manually: Yeh feature Django khud nahi deta, tumhe copy.deepcopy() ya manual clone logic likhna padega.

Sawal 3: Kaunse Patterns Overuse Nahi Karne Chahiye?
1. Abstract Factory
Kya hai: Multiple related object families banane ka tareeqa (jaise ek factory jo alag-alag "themes" ke sets banaye).
Kyun avoid karein: Job Board jaisi chhoti-medium app mein humein aisi zaroorat nahi ke hum multiple related object families create karein — yeh unnecessary complexity add karega bina kisi real fayde ke.
2. Flyweight
Kya hai: Bohot saare similar objects ke beech memory share karna (jaise game mein hazaron trees ka texture share karna).
Kyun avoid karein: Web request/response cycle mein aam taur pe itni memory-heavy repetition nahi hoti ke Flyweight ki zaroorat pade — yeh pattern game development ya bohot large-scale simulations ke liye zyada relevant hai.
3. Visitor
Kya hai: Naye operations add karna without modifying existing classes, ek "visitor" object different classes pe different operations perform kare.
Kyun avoid karein: Python ka dynamic/duck-typing nature is pattern ki zaroorat hi kam kar deta hai — Python mein waise hi polymorphism aasan hai, is complex pattern ki zaroorat rarely padti hai.
4. Composite
Kya hai: Tree-like structure banana jahan individual aur group objects ko same tareeqe se treat kiya ja sake (jaise folder ke andar files aur sub-folders).
Kyun avoid karein: Sirf tab use karo jab genuinely recursive/nested hierarchy ho (jaise nested job categories: Tech → Software → Backend). Agar Job Board mein aisi hierarchy nahi hai, to isko force-fit karna galat hoga.
5. Bridge
Kya hai: Abstraction aur implementation ko alag rakhna taake dono independently badal sakein.
Kyun avoid karein: Yeh Strategy pattern se kaafi overlap karta hai. Agar tum already Strategy use kar rahe ho (jaise notification channels ke liye), to Bridge dobara use karna redundant hoga — dono ka concept bohot similar hai
